ealer firms in the United States, the United Kingdom, and internationally. The company offers trading technology to access liquidity on its platforms in U.S. high-grade bonds, U.S. high-yield bonds, emerging market debt, eurobonds, municipal bonds, U.S. government bonds, and other fixed-income securities; and executes bond trades between and among institutional investor and broker-dealer clients in an all-to-all anonymous trading environment for corporate bonds through its Open Trading protocols. It also provides automated and algorithmic trading solutions, such as X-Pro, a trading platform to combine trading protocols with its proprietary data and pre-trade analytics; and integrated and actionable data offerings, including CP+ and Axess All, a real-time pricing engine, including Auto-X and portfolio trading. In addition, the company offers various pre-and post-trade services, such as processing, trade matching, trade publication, regulatory transaction reporting, and market and reference data across a range of fixed-income and other products. The company was incorporated in 2000 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher Robert Concannon J.D. | CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 858 people. Revenue per employee of $986K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $436K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $36K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["MarketAxess Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $5.8B market cap on $846M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 33% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 24-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $374M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 44 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.55\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 9.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.02541845704669734},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","16 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"MarketAxess Holdings Inc. $MKTX Stock: New York Life Investment Management LLC Boosts Holdings","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/16/marketaxess-holdings-inc-mktx-stock-new-york-life-investment-management-llc-boosts-holdings.html","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794830744.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.888,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The CEO Who Owns the NYSE Just Sold $32 Million of Stock","source":"247wallst.com","link":"https://247wallst.com/investing/2026/11/20/the-ceo-who-owns-the-nyse-just-sold-32-million-of-stock/","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795195376.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"CME Group Stock And Other Exchange Operators Leveraged To AI Trading","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/options/articles/cme-group-stock-other-exchange-121358083.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795176838.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Inside George Soros\u2019s Portfolio: Every Move He Made in the Third Quarter","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"h